const Q_L1 = [
/* ===================== q1 · Sintaxis y formalización (L1) ===================== */
{t:"q1",x:"Simulacro 2",m:1,q:"Select the correct answers (there could be more than one):",o:["∀x (∀x A(x) ∧ ∃y B(x,y) → ∀x C(x)) is a bound formula.","∀x (A(x) ∧ B(x,y)) → ¬C(f(y), y) is a well formed formula.","∀x (P(x) ∧ Q(¬f(x))) is a well formed formula.","∀x ∃y A(x,y) ∧ B(x,y) is a bound formula."],a:[0,1],e:"a) todas las apariciones de x e y están en el ámbito de un cuantificador suyo. b) está bien formada aunque y quede libre. c) ¬ no se aplica a términos: ¬f(x) no es nada. d) los cuantificadores tienen la máxima prioridad, así que el ámbito de ∀x∃y es solo A(x,y) y en B(x,y) x e y están libres."},
{t:"q1",x:"Simulacro 1",q:"Formalize, using person(x): x is a person, loves(x,y): x loves y: “There are people who love a person only if that person loves them”.",o:["∃x (person(x) ∧ ∃y (loves(x,y) ∧ loves(y,x)))","∃x (person(x) ∧ ∀y (loves(y,x) → loves(x,y)))","∃x (person(x) ∧ ∃y (loves(y,x) → loves(x,y)))","∃x (person(x) ∧ ∀y (loves(x,y) → loves(y,x)))"],a:3,e:"«x loves y only if y loves x» = loves(x,y) → loves(y,x), para cualquier y. b) es la implicación al revés y c) usa ∃ con →, que casi siempre es un error."},
{t:"q1",x:"Simulacro 2",q:"Formalize, using Student(x), Professor(x), Passes(x), ExplainsWell(x): “For all students to pass it is necessary that some professor explains well”.",o:["∃x (Professor(x) ∧ ExplainsWell(x)) → ∀x (Student(x) → Passes(x))","∃x (Professor(x) ∧ ExplainsWell(x)) → ∀x (Student(x) ∧ Passes(x))","∀x (Student(x) ∧ Passes(x)) → ∃x (Professor(x) ∧ ExplainsWell(x))","∀x (Student(x) → Passes(x)) → ∃x (Professor(x) ∧ ExplainsWell(x))"],a:3,e:"«B is necessary for A» = A → B, con A = «todos los estudiantes aprueban» = ∀x (Student(x) → Passes(x)) y B = ∃x (Professor(x) ∧ ExplainsWell(x)). c) usa ∀ con ∧ («todo el mundo es estudiante y aprueba»)."},
{t:"q1",x:"Simulacro 3",q:"With Psychologist(x), Loves(x,y): x loves y, Helps(x,y): x helps y, which sentence corresponds to ∃x (Psychologist(x) ∧ ∀y (¬Loves(y,y) → Helps(x,y)))?",o:["Some psychologists help some people who do not love themselves.","None of the others is correct.","Some psychologists help all the people who do not love themselves.","Some psychologists help only the people who do not love themselves."],a:2,ns:1,e:"∀y (¬Loves(y,y) → Helps(x,y)): todo el que no se quiere a sí mismo es ayudado por x. «Only» sería Helps(x,y) → ¬Loves(y,y), la implicación al revés."},
{t:"q1",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"Formalize, using A(X): X is an author, W(X): X writes well, R(X,Y): X reads Y: “Not all authors write well. However, authors that write well are read by somebody.”",o:["¬∀X (A(X) → W(X)) ∧ ∀X (A(X) ∧ W(X) → ∃Y R(Y,X))","¬∀X (A(X) → W(X)) ∧ ∀X (A(X) ∧ W(X) → ∃Y R(X,Y))","∀X ¬(A(X) → W(X)) ∧ ∀X (A(X) ∧ W(X) → ∃Y R(Y,X))","¬∀X (A(X) ∧ W(X)) ∧ ∃Y ∀X (A(X) ∧ W(X) → R(Y,X))"],a:0,e:"R(X,Y) es «X lee a Y», así que «X es leído por alguien» es ∃Y R(Y,X). c) diría que ningún autor escribe bien. d) niega «todo el mundo es un autor que escribe bien» y además exige un mismo lector para todos."},
{t:"q1",x:"Examen 19/20",q:"Formalize, using P(x,y): x plays y, L(x): x likes sports, a: soccer: “All those who play soccer like sports, however not all those who like sports play soccer”.",o:["∀x (P(x,a) → L(x)) ∧ ∃x (L(x) ∧ ¬P(x,a))","∀x (P(x,a) → L(x)) ∧ ¬∃x (L(x) → P(x,a))","∀x (L(x) → P(x,a)) ∧ ∃x (L(x) ∧ ¬P(x,a))","∀x (P(x,a) ∧ L(x)) ∧ ¬∀x (L(x) → P(x,a))"],a:0,e:"«Not all who like sports play soccer» = ¬∀x (L(x) → P(x,a)) ≡ ∃x (L(x) ∧ ¬P(x,a)). b) ¬∃x (L → P) diría que todo el mundo cumple L y no juega."},
{t:"q1",q:"“All p are q” is formalized as:",o:["∀X (p(X) → q(X))","∀X (p(X) ∧ q(X))","∃X (p(X) → q(X))","∀X (q(X) → p(X))"],a:0,e:"El cuantificador universal suele ir con →. b) diría que todo es p y q. d) es «only p are q»."},
{t:"q1",q:"“Only p are q” is formalized as:",o:["∀X (q(X) → p(X))","∀X (p(X) → q(X))","∃X (p(X) ∧ q(X))","∀X (p(X) ∧ q(X))"],a:0,e:"Si algo es q, entonces es p. Igual que «only if» en L0: lo que sigue a «only» va en el consecuente."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"Which formulas formalize “No p is q”? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X (p(X) → ¬q(X))","¬∃X (p(X) ∧ q(X))","∀X (¬p(X) → ¬q(X))","¬∀X (p(X) → q(X))"],a:[0,1],e:"Las dos formas del tema: «todo p no es q» o «no existe un p que sea q». d) es «no todos los p son q»."},
{t:"q1",q:"“Some p are q” is formalized as:",o:["∃X (p(X) ∧ q(X))","∃X (p(X) → q(X))","∀X (p(X) ∧ q(X))","∃X p(X) ∧ ∃X q(X)"],a:0,e:"El existencial suele ir con ∧. d) dice que hay p y hay q, quizá distintos."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"With D(X): X is a dog, H(X): X is a human, F(X,Y): X is friend of Y, which formulas formalize “There are some dogs that are not friends of any human”? (there could be more than one)",o:["∃X [D(X) ∧ ¬∃Y (H(Y) ∧ F(X,Y))]","∃X [D(X) ∧ ∀Y (H(Y) → ¬F(X,Y))]","∃X [D(X) ∧ ∃Y (H(Y) ∧ ¬F(X,Y))]","∃X [D(X) → ∀Y (H(Y) → ¬F(X,Y))]"],a:[0,1],e:"Son las dos soluciones del tema. c) solo dice que hay un humano del que no es amigo y d) usa ∃ con →."},
{t:"q1",q:"With D(X): X is a dog, H(X): X is a human, F(X,Y): X is friend of Y, “Dogs are only friends of humans” is:",o:["∀X [D(X) → ∀Y (F(X,Y) → H(Y))]","∀X [D(X) → ∀Y (H(Y) → F(X,Y))]","∀X ∀Y [D(X) ∧ H(Y) → F(X,Y)]","∀X [D(X) → ∃Y (H(Y) ∧ F(X,Y))]"],a:0,e:"Si un perro es amigo de Y, Y es humano. b) y c) son «dogs are friends of humans» (de todos)."},
{t:"q1",q:"With D(X): X is a dragon, F(X): X is a flea, H(X,Y): X hounds Y, “Every flea hounds some dragon” is:",o:["∀Y [F(Y) → ∃X (D(X) ∧ H(Y,X))]","∃X [D(X) ∧ ∀Y (F(Y) → H(Y,X))]","∀Y [F(Y) ∧ ∃X (D(X) ∧ H(Y,X))]","∀Y [F(Y) → ∃X (D(X) → H(Y,X))]"],a:0,e:"b) diría que hay un dragón acosado por todas las pulgas (más fuerte)."},
{t:"q1",q:"With D(X): X is a dragon, F(X): X is a flea, H(X,Y): X hounds Y, “Some fleas hound all dragons” is:",o:["∃Y [F(Y) ∧ ∀X (D(X) → H(Y,X))]","∃Y [F(Y) → ∀X (D(X) → H(Y,X))]","∀X [D(X) → ∃Y (F(Y) ∧ H(Y,X))]","∃Y [F(Y) ∧ ∀X (D(X) ∧ H(Y,X))]"],a:0,e:"∃ con ∧ y ∀ con →. d) diría que todo es un dragón."},
{t:"q1",q:"With D(X): X is a dragon, F(X): X is a flea, H(X,Y): X hounds Y, “Some dragons are hounded by all fleas” is:",o:["∃X [D(X) ∧ ∀Y (F(Y) → H(Y,X))]","∃X [D(X) ∧ ∀Y (F(Y) → H(X,Y))]","∀Y [F(Y) → ∃X (D(X) ∧ H(Y,X))]","∃X ∀Y [D(X) ∧ F(Y) ∧ H(Y,X)]"],a:0,e:"H(Y,X) = Y acosa a X: el dragón es el segundo argumento. c) es «every flea hounds some dragon»."},
{t:"q1",q:"With D(X): X is a dragon, F(X): X is a flea, H(X,Y): X hounds Y, “Every dragon is hounded by some flea” is:",o:["∀X [D(X) → ∃Y (F(Y) ∧ H(Y,X))]","∃Y [F(Y) ∧ ∀X (D(X) → H(Y,X))]","∀X [D(X) → ∃Y (F(Y) → H(Y,X))]","∀X ∃Y [D(X) ∧ F(Y) → H(X,Y)]"],a:0,e:"Para cada dragón hay una pulga (puede ser distinta para cada uno). b) es «some flea hounds all dragons»."},
{t:"q1",q:"With P(X,Y): X and Y are partners, E(X): X has a fever, “If your partner has a fever then you do too” is:",o:["∀X [∃Y (P(X,Y) ∧ E(Y)) → E(X)]","∀X ∃Y [P(X,Y) ∧ E(Y) ∧ E(X)]","∃X [∀Y (P(X,Y) → E(Y)) → E(X)]","∀X [E(X) → ∃Y (P(X,Y) ∧ E(Y))]"],a:0,e:"Para todo X: si existe una pareja Y con fiebre, X tiene fiebre (solución del tema)."},
{t:"q1",q:"With P(X,Y): X can play the piece Y, Q(X): X practices, G(X): X is a great musician, “Only great musicians can play a piece without practicing” is:",o:["∀X [∃Y (P(X,Y) ∧ ¬Q(X)) → G(X)]","∀X [G(X) → ∃Y (P(X,Y) ∧ ¬Q(X))]","∀X ∀Y [P(X,Y) → G(X) ∧ ¬Q(X)]","∃X [G(X) ∧ ∃Y (P(X,Y) ∧ ¬Q(X))]"],a:0,e:"«Only G can do A» = A → G. Es la primera premisa del ejercicio de los músicos del tema."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"With E(X,Y): X enrolls in the course Y and the constant peter, which formulas formalize “Peter has not enrolled in any course”? (there could be more than one)",o:["¬∃X E(peter,X)","∀X ¬E(peter,X)","∃X ¬E(peter,X)","¬∀X E(peter,X)"],a:[0,1],e:"«Ningún X verifica P» = ∀X ¬P(X) = ¬∃X P(X). c) y d) dicen que hay algún curso en el que no se ha matriculado."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"With G(X): X is a green piece, R(X): X is a red piece, B(X,Y): X is beside Y, which formulas formalize “No green piece is beside a red piece”? (there could be more than one)",o:["¬∃X (G(X) ∧ ∃Y (R(Y) ∧ B(X,Y)))","∀X (G(X) → ∀Y (B(X,Y) → ¬R(Y)))","∀X ∀Y (G(X) ∧ R(Y) → ¬B(X,Y))","∀X (G(X) → ∃Y (R(Y) ∧ ¬B(X,Y)))"],a:[0,1,2],e:"Son las tres soluciones del tema. d) solo dice que cada pieza verde tiene alguna roja que no está a su lado."},
{t:"q1",q:"With G(X): green piece, L(X): blue piece, B(X,Y): X is beside Y, “Some green piece is beside all blue pieces” is:",o:["∃X (G(X) ∧ ∀Y (L(Y) → B(X,Y)))","∃X (G(X) ∧ ∀Y (L(Y) ∧ B(X,Y)))","∀Y (L(Y) → ∃X (G(X) ∧ B(X,Y)))","∃X ∀Y (G(X) → L(Y) ∧ B(X,Y))"],a:0,e:"c) permite una pieza verde distinta para cada azul."},
{t:"q1",q:"With O(X): orange piece, R(X): red piece, L(X): blue piece, B(X,Y): X is beside Y, “All the orange pieces beside a red piece are beside a blue piece” is:",o:["∀X (O(X) ∧ ∃Y (R(Y) ∧ B(X,Y)) → ∃Z (L(Z) ∧ B(X,Z)))","∀X (O(X) → ∃Y (R(Y) ∧ B(X,Y)) ∧ ∃Z (L(Z) ∧ B(X,Z)))","∀X ∃Y (O(X) ∧ R(Y) ∧ B(X,Y) → ∀Z (L(Z) → B(X,Z)))","∃X (O(X) ∧ ∃Y (R(Y) ∧ B(X,Y)) ∧ ∃Z (L(Z) ∧ B(X,Z)))"],a:0,e:"El antecedente es «X es naranja y está al lado de alguna roja»; el consecuente, «está al lado de alguna azul». b) afirma que todas las naranjas tienen una roja al lado."},
{t:"q1",q:"With Lives(X,Y): X lives in Y, “Everybody lives somewhere” is:",o:["∀X ∃Y Lives(X,Y)","∃Y ∀X Lives(X,Y)","∀X ∀Y Lives(X,Y)","∃X ∃Y Lives(X,Y)"],a:0,e:"b) diría que hay un sitio donde vive todo el mundo: cambiar el orden de ∀ y ∃ cambia el significado."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"Which of the following are bound formulas (without free variables)? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) → q(X,a,Y))","∀X (∃Y p(X,Y) → q(X,Y))","∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) ∧ q(X,Z) → r(f(X)))","∀X p(X) ∧ q(a)"],a:[0,3],e:"b) la Y de q(X,Y) está fuera del ámbito de ∃Y. c) Z no está cuantificada. a es una constante, no una variable."},
{t:"q1",q:"In ∀X ∃Y p(X,Y) → ¬∃X q(X) ∧ r(X,f(X)), what is the scope of ∀X?",o:["∃Y p(X,Y)","∃Y p(X,Y) → ¬∃X q(X) ∧ r(X,f(X))","p(X,Y)","q(X)"],a:0,e:"Los cuantificadores tienen la máxima prioridad: sin paréntesis, ∀X solo alcanza a ∃Y p(X,Y). Es el ejemplo del tema."},
{t:"q1",q:"In ∀X ∃Y p(X,Y) → ¬∃X q(X) ∧ r(X,f(X)), the variable X…",o:["appears bound twice and free twice (in r(X,f(X)))","is bound everywhere","is free everywhere","is bound only by ∃X"],a:0,ns:1,e:"Ligada en ∀X ∃Y p(X,Y) y en ¬∃X q(X); libre en r(X,f(X)), fuera de ambos ámbitos."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"Let f be a function symbol, p and q predicate symbols, a a constant and X, Y variables. Which of the following are terms? (there could be more than one)",o:["f(X,a)","X","q(f(X,Y))","p(a) ∧ q(X)"],a:[0,1],e:"Términos: constantes, variables y funciones aplicadas a términos. Al evaluarlos dan un objeto, no un valor de verdad. q(f(X,Y)) es una fórmula atómica."},
{t:"q1",q:"Let P and Q be predicate symbols and f a function symbol. Which expression is NOT well formed?",o:["P(Q(X))","P(f(X))","¬P(X) ∨ Q(f(f(X)))","∀X P(X) → Q(a)"],a:0,e:"Los argumentos de un predicado son términos, y Q(X) es una fórmula."},
{t:"q1",q:"An occurrence of a variable is free when:",o:["It is not in the scope of any quantifier on that variable","It appears inside a function","It appears only once","It is quantified by ∃"],a:0,e:"Libre = no cuantificada; ligada = en el ámbito de un ∀ o ∃ sobre esa variable."},
{t:"q1",q:"The arity of a predicate or function symbol is:",o:["Its number of arguments","The number of times it appears","Its depth in the syntax tree","The number of quantifiers that affect it"],a:0,e:"p(X,Y) tiene aridad 2. Los predicados de aridad 0 son proposiciones."},
{t:"q1",q:"When formalizing a sentence in predicate logic, the resulting formula must be:",o:["A bound (closed) formula, without free variables","A formula in clausal form","A formula without existential quantifiers","A formula with every quantifier at the beginning"],a:0,e:"Nota del tema: el resultado de formalizar debe ser una fórmula cerrada."},
{t:"q1",q:"With S(X): X is a student, T(X): X studies, P(X): X passes, “Every student who studies passes” is:",o:["∀X (S(X) ∧ T(X) → P(X))","∀X (S(X) ∧ T(X) ∧ P(X))","∃X (S(X) ∧ T(X) → P(X))","∀X (S(X) → T(X) ∧ P(X))"],a:0,e:"d) diría que todos los estudiantes estudian y aprueban."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"With S(X): X is a student and P(X): X passes, which formulas formalize “Not every student passes”? (there could be more than one)",o:["¬∀X (S(X) → P(X))","∃X (S(X) ∧ ¬P(X))","∀X (S(X) → ¬P(X))","∃X (S(X) → ¬P(X))"],a:[0,1],e:"¬∀X G ≡ ∃X ¬G, y ¬(S → P) ≡ S ∧ ¬P. c) es «ningún estudiante aprueba»."},
{t:"q1",q:"With L(X,Y): X loves Y, “Someone is loved by everybody” is:",o:["∃Y ∀X L(X,Y)","∀X ∃Y L(X,Y)","∃X ∀Y L(X,Y)","∀Y ∃X L(X,Y)"],a:0,e:"Hay un Y tal que todo X lo quiere. c) es «alguien quiere a todo el mundo»."},
{t:"q1",q:"With S(X): X is a student, B(X): X is a book, R(X,Y): X reads Y, which sentence corresponds to ∀X (S(X) → ∃Y (B(Y) ∧ R(X,Y)))?",o:["Every student reads some book.","Some book is read by every student.","Every student reads every book.","Some student reads some book."],a:0,e:"Para cada estudiante hay un libro (que puede ser distinto)."},
{t:"q1",q:"With S(X): X is a student, B(X): X is a book, R(X,Y): X reads Y, which sentence corresponds to ∃X (S(X) ∧ ∀Y (B(Y) → R(X,Y)))?",o:["Some student reads every book.","Every student reads some book.","Some book is read by every student.","Every book is read by some student."],a:0,e:"∃ con ∧ para el estudiante y ∀ con → para los libros."},
{t:"q1",q:"With m(X): the mother of X (a function), P(X): X is a person, L(X,Y): X loves Y, “Every person is loved by their mother” is:",o:["∀X (P(X) → L(m(X),X))","∀X (P(X) → L(X,m(X)))","∀X ∃Y (P(X) → L(Y,X))","∀X (P(X) → m(L(X)))"],a:0,e:"Las funciones se refieren a objetos de forma indirecta. d) aplica una función a una fórmula: no está bien formada."},
{t:"q1",q:"With a: John, f(X): the mother of X, p(X): X plays poker, q(X): X studies Informatics, r(X): X is stubborn, “All the mothers of Informatics students that play poker are stubborn; besides, John studies Informatics” is:",o:["∀X (p(X) ∧ q(X) → r(f(X))) ∧ q(a)","∀X (p(f(X)) ∧ q(f(X)) → r(X)) ∧ q(a)","∀X (p(X) ∧ q(X) → r(X)) ∧ q(f(a))","∀X (r(f(X)) → p(X) ∧ q(X)) ∧ q(a)"],a:0,e:"Es la interpretación J del ejemplo del tema: la misma fórmula, con otra interpretación, habla de cuadrados de números impares."},
{t:"q1",q:"With F(X): X has the flu and E(X): X has a fever, “Everyone with the flu has a fever” is:",o:["∀X (F(X) → E(X))","∀X (F(X) ∧ E(X))","∃X (F(X) ∧ E(X))","∀X (E(X) → F(X))"],a:0,e:"Regla típica: ∀ con →."},
{t:"q1",q:"With B(X): X is a Barbarian, E(X): X drinks beer, W(X): X drinks whisky, “There are non Barbarians who drink beer or whisky” is:",o:["∃X (¬B(X) ∧ (E(X) ∨ W(X)))","∃X (¬B(X) → E(X) ∨ W(X))","¬∃X (B(X) ∧ (E(X) ∨ W(X)))","∀X (¬B(X) → E(X) ∨ W(X))"],a:0,e:"Existencial con ∧. b) se cumpliría con cualquier bárbaro."},
{t:"q1",q:"Which formula does NOT formalize “All dolphins are mammals”?",o:["∀X (dolphin(X) ∧ mammal(X))","∀X (dolphin(X) → mammal(X))","¬∃X (dolphin(X) ∧ ¬mammal(X))","∀X (¬mammal(X) → ¬dolphin(X))"],a:0,e:"a) dice que todo es un delfín mamífero. c) y d) son equivalentes a b) (De Morgan con cuantificadores y contraposición)."},
{t:"q1",q:"In the formula ∀X p(X) → q(X):",o:["The scope of ∀X is only p(X), so X is free in q(X)","The scope of ∀X is p(X) → q(X)","It is not a well formed formula","q(X) is bound by an implicit ∃X"],a:0,e:"Sin paréntesis, el cuantificador solo afecta a la fórmula atómica que le sigue."},
{t:"q1",q:"In ∀X (p(X) → ∃X q(X)), the X of q(X) is quantified by:",o:["∃X, the closest quantifier","∀X, the outermost quantifier","Both quantifiers","None: it is free"],a:0,e:"Si una variable está en el ámbito de varios cuantificadores, la cuantifica el más cercano."},
{t:"q1",q:"Why is ∃X (cow(X) → good(X)) a bad formalization of “Some cows are good”?",o:["It is true as soon as something is not a cow, even if no cow is good","It says that every cow is good","It is not a well formed formula","It needs a universal quantifier inside"],a:0,e:"∃X (A → B) es verdadera si existe un X con A falso. Por eso el existencial se usa con ∧."},
{t:"q1",q:"Why can't propositional logic prove “All dogs are good, Bobby is a dog; therefore, Bobby is good”?",o:["It cannot talk about properties of individuals: the three sentences become unrelated propositions p, q, r","Because the reasoning is not sound","Because it has no implication","It can: {p, q} ⊨ r is sound"],a:0,e:"En L1: {∀X (p(X) → q(X)), p(bobby)} ⊨ q(bobby), que sí es correcto."},
{t:"q1",m:1,q:"Which elements does predicate logic add to propositional logic? (there could be more than one)",o:["Predicates, constants and functions","Variables and quantifiers","New connectives","Truth values other than T and F"],a:[0,1],e:"Las conectivas son las mismas y sigue habiendo solo dos valores de verdad."},
{t:"q1",q:"Which sentence corresponds to ∀X (Student(X) ∧ Smart(X))?",o:["Everyone is a student and is smart.","All students are smart.","Some students are smart.","Only students are smart."],a:0,e:"Un ∀ con ∧ casi nunca es lo que se quiere decir: afirma algo de todo el dominio."},

/* ===================== q2 · Semántica (L1) ===================== */
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 1",q:"Indicate the correct option:",o:["∀y ∃x A(x,y) ⊨ ∃x ∀y A(x,y)","∃x ∀y A(x,y) ⊨ ∀y ∃x A(x,y)","∀x (A(x) ∨ B(x)) ⊨ ∀x A(x) ∨ ∀x B(x)","∃x A(x) ∧ ∃x B(x) ⊨ ∃x (A(x) ∧ B(x))"],a:1,e:"Si hay un x que cumple A(x,y) para todo y, ese mismo x sirve para cada y. a), c) y d) son las tres implicaciones que el tema dice que no se cumplen."},
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 3",q:"Select the INCORRECT answer:",o:["∀x ∀y A(x,y) ⊨ ∀y ∀x A(x,y)","∃x A(x) ∧ ∃x B(x) ⊨ ∃x (A(x) ∧ B(x))","∃x A(x) ∨ ∃x B(x) ⊨ ∃x (A(x) ∨ B(x))","∀x (A(x) ∧ B(x)) ⊨ ∀x A(x) ∧ ∀x B(x)"],a:1,e:"Contraejemplo del tema: hay estudiantes y hay trabajadores, pero puede no haber estudiantes que trabajen."},
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 1",m:1,q:"Consider the interpretation I = { D = {1,2,3}, p(x) = “x equals 1”, q(x,y) = “x is less than or equal to y” }. Select the formulas that are true under I (there could be more than one):",o:["¬∃x ∃y (p(x) ↔ (q(y,x) → p(y)))","¬∀x ¬∀y (p(x) ↔ (q(y,x) → p(y)))","∃x ¬∃y (p(x) ↔ (q(y,x) → p(y)))","∃x ¬∀y (p(x) ↔ (q(y,x) → p(y)))"],a:[1,3],v:["L1",{D:[1,2,3],c:{},f:{},p:{p:x=>x===1,q:(x,y)=>x<=y}}],e:"Llamemos K(x,y) al núcleo. Para x = 1, K es T con todo y; para x = 2 solo con y = 2; para x = 3 con y = 2 y y = 3. b) ≡ ∃x ∀y K: x = 1 ✔. d) x = 2 falla con y = 1 ✔. a) es F porque K se cumple alguna vez. c) es F porque para cada x hay algún y con K."},
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 2",m:1,q:"Given the interpretation I = { D = {1,2,3}, P(x,y) = “x is less than or equal to y”, Q(x) = “x equals 3” }, select the formulas that are true under I (there could be several correct answers):",o:["∀y ∀x (P(x,y) → Q(y))","∀y ∃x (P(x,y) → Q(y))","∃y ∀x (P(x,y) ∧ Q(y))","∀y ∃x (P(x,y) ∧ Q(y))"],a:[1,2],v:["L1",{D:[1,2,3],c:{},f:{},p:{P:(x,y)=>x<=y,Q:x=>x===3}}],e:"a) falla con x = y = 1. b) para y = 1 sirve x = 2 (P falso), para y = 2 x = 3, para y = 3 Q(3) es T. c) y = 3: todo x ≤ 3 y Q(3). d) falla con y = 1 porque Q(1) es F."},
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 2",m:1,q:"Given F₁: ∀y ∃x (R(x) → (P(x,y) ↔ Q(y))) and F₂: ∃y ∀x (R(x) → (P(x,y) ↔ Q(y))), and the interpretation I = { D = {1,2}, Q(x) = “x ≤ 1”, R(x) = “x ≤ 2”, P(x,y) = ? }, complete I so that F₁ is false and F₂ is true (there could be several correct answers).",o:["P(x,y) = “x is less than or equal to 2”","P(x,y) = “x is less than or equal to y”","P(x,y) = “y is less than or equal to 0”","P(x,y) = “x does not equal y”"],a:[0,2],e:"R siempre es T, así que el núcleo es P(x,y) ↔ Q(y). a) P siempre T: queda Q(y); F₁ = ∀y Q(y) = F y F₂ = ∃y Q(y) = T ✔. c) P siempre F: queda ¬Q(y), F₁ F y F₂ T ✔. b) da F₂ falsa. d) da F₁ verdadera."},
{t:"q2",x:"Simulacro 3",m:1,q:"Consider the formula ∃x ∀y (A(x,y) ∧ B(x) → C(y)). Select which of the following interpretations make the formula true (there could be several correct answers):",o:["Dom: {1,2}, A(x,y): x is greater than or equal to y, B(x): x is less than 3, C(x): x is even","Dom: {ant, dog, elephant}, A(x,y): x is bigger than y, B(x): x has exactly 4 legs, C(x): x has a trunk","Dom: {1,2}, A(x,y): x less than or equal to y, B(x): x is odd, C(x): x is even","Dom: {A}, A(x,y): {(A,A)}, B(x): {A}, C(x): {}"],a:[1,2],e:"Basta un x que haga falso B(x): con x = ant (6 patas) en b) o x = 2 (par) en c), el antecedente es F para todo y. En a) cualquier x falla con y = 1 (no par). En d) A(A,A) ∧ B(A) es T y C(A) F."},
{t:"q2",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"Evaluate ∀Y¬∀X (p(X,Y) → q(X) ∨ r(Y)) under D = {1,2}, p(X,Y) = “X ≥ Y”, q(X) = “X is odd”, r(X) = “X > 5”:",o:["True: for Y = 1 and Y = 2, ∀X(…) is false because X = 2 falsifies the implication","False: for Y = 1, X = 1 makes the implication true","True: every instance of the implication is true","False: r(X) is never true"],a:0,ns:1,v:["self","true","∀Y¬∀X (p(X,Y) → q(X) ∨ r(Y))",{D:[1,2],c:{},f:{},p:{p:(x,y)=>x>=y,q:x=>x%2===1,r:x=>x>5}}],e:"Árbol AND/OR de la solución oficial: con X = 2, p(2,Y) es T y q(2) ∨ r(Y) es F, así que ∀X(…) es F para Y = 1 y para Y = 2; el ¬ lo convierte en T en ambas ramas y el ∀Y da T."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {0,1,2} and p(X,Y) = “there is an arrow from X to Y” in the graph with arrows 0→1, 1→0, 1→2, 2→0, 2→1 and 2→2. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X∀Y p(X,Y)","∃X∃Y p(X,Y)","∀X∃Y p(X,Y)","∃X∀Y p(X,Y)"],a:[1,2,3],v:["L1",GRAPH],e:"Ejercicio del grafo del tema. a) falla: no hay flecha 0→0. c) todo nodo tiene alguna flecha saliente. d) el nodo 2 tiene flechas a todos (incluido él mismo)."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {0,1,2} and p(X,Y) = “there is an arrow from X to Y” in the graph with arrows 0→1, 1→0, 1→2, 2→0, 2→1 and 2→2. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∃Y∀X p(X,Y)","∀Y∃X p(X,Y)","∀X p(X,X)","∃X p(X,X)"],a:[1,3],v:["L1",GRAPH],e:"a) ningún nodo recibe flechas de todos (a 0 no le llega 0→0). b) a todo nodo le llega alguna flecha. d) 2→2."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {1,2}, p(X,Y) = “X = Y”, q(X) = “X is odd”. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) → q(X))","∀X (∃Y p(X,Y) → q(X))","∃X∀Y (p(X,Y) → q(X))","∀X∀Y (p(X,Y) → q(X))"],a:[0,2],v:["L1",{D:[1,2],c:{},f:{},p:{p:(x,y)=>x===y,q:x=>x%2===1}}],e:"Ejercicio del tema: en a) para X = 2 vale Y = 1 (p falso); en b) ∃Y p(2,Y) es T y q(2) F. Moraleja: la posición del ∃ cambia el resultado."},
{t:"q2",q:"Let D = {1,2,3}, a = 1, b = 3, f(X) = 4 − X, g(X,Y,Z) = ((X + Y + Z) mod 3) + 1, p(X,Y) = “X ≤ Y”, q(X) = “X = 2 or X = 3”. Evaluate ∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) ∧ q(f(X)) → ¬q(g(a,b,f(Y)))):",o:["True","False"],a:0,ns:1,v:["self","true","∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) ∧ q(f(X)) → ¬q(g(a,b,f(Y))))",{D:[1,2,3],c:{a:1,b:3},f:{f:x=>4-x,g:(x,y,z)=>((x+y+z)%3)+1},p:{p:(x,y)=>x<=y,q:x=>x===2||x===3}}],e:"X = 1: con Y = 2, g(1,3,f(2)) = g(1,3,2) = 1 y ¬q(1) es T. X = 2 y X = 3: con Y = 1 el antecedente es F (p(2,1) F; q(f(3)) = q(1) F)."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let F = ∃Y¬∃X (p(Y) ↔ q(X,Y)), with D = {A,B} and p = {A}. For which interpretations of q is F true? (there could be more than one)",o:["q = {(A,B), (A,A), (B,B)}","q = {(A,B), (A,A)}","q = { } (empty)","q = {(B,A)}"],a:[0,2],v:["L1q"],e:"F es T si hay un Y para el que ningún X cumple p(Y) ↔ q(X,Y). a) con Y = B: p(B) = F y q(A,B), q(B,B) son T, así que ningún bicondicional se cumple ✔ (I₂ del tema). b) es I₁: F. c) con Y = A: p(A) = T y q(X,A) siempre F ✔."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"An interpretation I of a predicate logic formula consists of (select all that apply):",o:["A non-empty domain D","An element of D for each constant","A function Dⁿ → D for each n-ary function symbol and a function Dⁿ → {T, F} for each n-ary predicate","A truth value for each atomic formula, independent of the domain"],a:[0,1,2],e:"Definición del tema. El dominio nunca es vacío."},
{t:"q2",q:"Why can't truth tables be used to prove validity in predicate logic?",o:["Because a formula can have infinitely many interpretations","Because predicates have no truth value","Because quantifiers are not connectives","They can, with 2ⁿ rows"],a:0,e:"Hay infinitos dominios posibles (y dominios infinitos). Por eso se usan resolución general y deducción natural."},
{t:"q2",q:"¬∀X G(X) is equivalent to:",o:["∃X ¬G(X)","∀X ¬G(X)","¬∃X G(X)","∃X G(X)"],a:0,e:"De Morgan con cuantificadores: «no todos cumplen G» = «alguno no cumple G»."},
{t:"q2",q:"¬∃X G(X) is equivalent to:",o:["∀X ¬G(X)","∃X ¬G(X)","¬∀X G(X)","∀X G(X)"],a:0,e:"«No existe ninguno que cumpla G» = «ninguno cumple G»."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Select the logical equivalences that hold (there could be more than one):",o:["∀X (G(X) ∧ H(X)) ≡ ∀X G(X) ∧ ∀X H(X)","∃X (G(X) ∨ H(X)) ≡ ∃X G(X) ∨ ∃X H(X)","∀X (G(X) ∨ H(X)) ≡ ∀X G(X) ∨ ∀X H(X)","∃X (G(X) ∧ H(X)) ≡ ∃X G(X) ∧ ∃X H(X)"],a:[0,1],e:"∀ distribuye sobre ∧ y ∃ sobre ∨. Las otras dos solo valen en un sentido (⊨)."},
{t:"q2",q:"If X does not appear in H, which equivalence is NOT correct?",o:["H ∧ ∀X G(X) ≡ ∃X (H ∨ G(X))","H ∨ ∀X G(X) ≡ ∀X (H ∨ G(X))","H ∧ ∃X G(X) ≡ ∃X (H ∧ G(X))","H ∨ ∃X G(X) ≡ ∃X (H ∨ G(X))"],a:0,e:"Distributiva restringida: el cuantificador sale conservando su tipo y la conectiva. Es lo que se usa para mover cuantificadores a la izquierda."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Select the logical equivalences that hold (there could be more than one):",o:["∀X∀Y G(X,Y) ≡ ∀Y∀X G(X,Y)","∃X∃Y G(X,Y) ≡ ∃Y∃X G(X,Y)","∀X∃Y G(X,Y) ≡ ∃Y∀X G(X,Y)","∃X∀Y G(X,Y) ≡ ∀X∃Y G(X,Y)"],a:[0,1],e:"Cuantificadores del mismo tipo conmutan; ∀ y ∃ no."},
{t:"q2",q:"Which interpretation shows that ∀X (G(X) ∨ H(X)) ⊭ ∀X G(X) ∨ ∀X H(X)?",o:["G(X): X passes the exam, H(X): X fails the exam, with some students passing and some failing","G(X): X is a student, H(X): X is a worker, with some working students","G(X) and H(X) both “X is even” on D = {2,4}","Any interpretation where G is true for every element"],a:0,e:"Todos aprueban o suspenden, pero no es cierto que todos aprueben ni que todos suspendan."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Select the logical consequences that hold (there could be more than one):",o:["∀X G(X) ∨ ∀X H(X) ⊨ ∀X (G(X) ∨ H(X))","∃X (G(X) ∧ H(X)) ⊨ ∃X G(X) ∧ ∃X H(X)","∃X ∀Y G(X,Y) ⊨ ∀Y ∃X G(X,Y)","∀Y ∃X G(X,Y) ⊨ ∃X ∀Y G(X,Y)"],a:[0,1,2],e:"Tabla «It holds / It does not hold» del tema. d) falla: todo el mundo sale con alguien no implica que alguien salga con todos."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Select the valid formulas, true under every interpretation (there could be more than one):",o:["∀X p(X) → ∃X p(X)","∃X p(X) → ∀X p(X)","∀X (p(X) → q(X)) → (∀X p(X) → ∀X q(X))","∃X p(X) ∧ ∃X ¬p(X)"],a:[0,2],e:"a) es válida porque el dominio nunca es vacío. b) falla si solo algunos cumplen p. d) es satisfacible pero no válida."},
{t:"q2",q:"Which formula is unsatisfiable?",o:["∀X p(X) ∧ ∃X ¬p(X)","∃X p(X) ∧ ∃X ¬p(X)","∀X (p(X) ∨ ¬p(X))","∃X p(X) → ∀X p(X)"],a:0,e:"∃X ¬p(X) ≡ ¬∀X p(X): la conjunción es de la forma G ∧ ¬G. c) es válida."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {1,2,3}, cow(X) = “X = 1”, good(X) = “X = 3”. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∃X (cow(X) → good(X))","∃X (cow(X) ∧ good(X))","∀X (cow(X) → good(X))","∀X (good(X) → ¬cow(X))"],a:[0,3],v:["L1",{D:[1,2,3],c:{},f:{},p:{cow:x=>x===1,good:x=>x===3}}],e:"a) es T con X = 2, que no es una vaca, aunque ninguna vaca sea buena: por eso «some cows are good» se formaliza con ∧."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {1,2,3}, p(X,Y) = “X < Y”, e(X,Y) = “X = Y”. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X∃Y p(X,Y)","∃X∃Y p(X,Y)","∀Y∃X p(X,Y)","∃X∀Y (e(X,Y) ∨ p(X,Y))"],a:[1,3],v:["L1",{D:[1,2,3],c:{},f:{},p:{p:(x,y)=>x<y,e:(x,y)=>x===y}}],e:"a) falla con X = 3 y c) con Y = 1. d) X = 1 es menor o igual que todos."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {1,2}, f(X) = 3 − X and p(X) = “X = 1”. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X (p(X) ↔ ¬p(f(X)))","∃X p(f(X))","∀X p(f(f(X)))","∃X (p(X) ∧ p(f(X)))"],a:[0,1],v:["L1",{D:[1,2],c:{},f:{f:x=>3-x},p:{p:x=>x===1}}],e:"f intercambia 1 y 2, así que f(f(X)) = X: c) dice ∀X p(X), falso. a) p(1) y ¬p(2) son T; p(2) y ¬p(1) son F."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Let D = {A,B}, p = {A} and q = {(A,B), (B,B)}. Which formulas are true? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X∃Y q(X,Y)","∃Y∀X q(X,Y)","∀X (p(X) → ∃Y q(X,Y))","∃X (p(X) ∧ q(X,X))"],a:[0,1,2],v:["L1",{D:["A","B"],c:{},f:{},p:{p:x=>x==="A",q:(x,y)=>["A,B","B,B"].includes(x+","+y)}}],e:"Los dos nodos apuntan a B, así que a) y b) son T. d) falla: (A,A) no está en q."},
{t:"q2",q:"Let D = {1,2,3}, f(X) = 4 − X, p(X,Y) = “X ≤ Y”, q(X) = “X = 2 or X = 3”. Which formula is true?",o:["∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) → q(f(X)))","∀X∃Y (p(X,Y) ∧ q(f(X)))","∃Y∀X (p(X,Y) ∧ q(f(X)))","∀X (∃Y p(X,Y) → q(f(X)))"],a:0,v:["L1",{D:[1,2,3],c:{},f:{f:x=>4-x},p:{p:(x,y)=>x<=y,q:x=>x===2||x===3}}],e:"Ejercicio del tema. X = 3: q(f(3)) = q(1) es F, así que b), c) y d) fallan; en a) basta Y = 1, con p(3,1) falso."},
{t:"q2",q:"In the AND/OR tree used to evaluate a formula over a finite domain:",o:["A ∀ node is true if all its branches are true, and an ∃ node if at least one is","A ∀ node is true if at least one branch is true","Both quantifiers are AND nodes","Negations are ignored"],a:0,e:"∀ = nodo AND (una rama F basta para que sea F) y ∃ = nodo OR (una rama T basta para que sea T). Un ¬ invierte el resultado del subárbol."},
{t:"q2",q:"If ∀X F(X) is true under an interpretation I, then under I the formula ∃X F(X) is:",o:["True, because the domain is not empty","False","It depends on F","True only if F is valid"],a:0,e:"Por eso ∀X F(X) → ∃X F(X) es válida."},
{t:"q2",q:"Is ∃Y∀X loves(X,Y) ⊨ ∀X∃Y loves(X,Y) correct?",o:["Yes: if someone is loved by everybody, everybody loves someone","No: the quantifiers cannot be exchanged","Yes, and the converse also holds","No, because loves is not symmetric"],a:0,e:"El Y que todos quieren sirve como «alguien» para cada X. Al revés no: cada uno puede querer a alguien distinto."},
{t:"q2",q:"Classify ∃X p(X) → ∀X p(X):",o:["Satisfiable but not valid","Valid","Unsatisfiable"],a:0,ns:1,e:"Es T si nadie o todos cumplen p (por ejemplo, con un dominio de un elemento) y F si solo algunos lo cumplen."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Which formulas express “No X verifies P”? (there could be more than one)",o:["∀X ¬P(X)","¬∃X P(X)","∃X ¬P(X)","¬∀X P(X)"],a:[0,1],e:"c) y d) expresan «algún X no verifica P»."},
{t:"q2",m:1,q:"Which formulas express “Some X does not verify P”? (there could be more than one)",o:["∃X ¬P(X)","¬∀X P(X)","∀X ¬P(X)","¬∃X P(X)"],a:[0,1],e:"Relación entre cuantificadores del tema."},
{t:"q2",q:"Under D = {1,2} and p(X) = “X is even”, ∀X p(X) is false because:",o:["The ∀ is an AND node and the branch X = 1 is F","The ∃ branch X = 2 is T","Every branch is F","Formulas with only one variable cannot be evaluated"],a:0,e:"Para un ∀ basta una rama falsa."},
{t:"q2",q:"Two formulas G and H of predicate logic are equivalent when:",o:["Gᴵ = Hᴵ for every interpretation I","Gᴵ = Hᴵ for some interpretation I","Both are satisfiable","They have the same predicates"],a:0,e:"Igual que en L0, y siguen valiendo todas las leyes de equivalencia proposicionales."},

/* ===================== q3 · Forma clausal, unificación y resolución general ===================== */
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"Obtain the clausal form of ∀Y [¬∃X r(f(X),Y) → ¬∃Z (q(Z) ∨ p(Y,Z))]:",o:["{r(f(g(Y)),Y) ∨ ¬q(Z), r(f(g(Y)),Y) ∨ ¬p(Y,Z)}","{r(f(a),Y) ∨ ¬q(Z), r(f(a),Y) ∨ ¬p(Y,Z)}","{¬r(f(X),Y) ∨ ¬q(Z) ∨ ¬p(Y,Z)}","{r(f(g(Y)),Y), ¬q(Z), ¬p(Y,Z)}"],a:0,e:"Eliminar →: ∀Y [∃X r(f(X),Y) ∨ ¬∃Z (…)]. ¬ hacia dentro: ∀Z (¬q(Z) ∧ ¬p(Y,Z)). Prenexa: ∀Y∃X∀Z. Skolem X/g(Y), porque ∃X está en el ámbito de ∀Y. Distributiva: dos cláusulas."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"In that conversion, why is X replaced by g(Y) and not by a constant?",o:["Because ∃X is in the scope of ∀Y (prefix ∀Y∃X∀Z)","Because X appears inside the function f","Because Z is universal","Because g is the next free function symbol"],a:0,e:"La función de Skolem depende de los ∀ que tiene a su izquierda. Sin ninguno sería una constante."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 3",q:"The clausal form of the formula ∀x (∃y (P(x,y) ∨ Q(y)) → ∃x Q(x)) would be:",o:["The set of clauses: {¬P(x,y) ∨ Q(f(x,y)), ¬Q(y) ∨ Q(f(x,y))}","The set of clauses: {¬P(x,y), ¬Q(y) ∨ Q(f(x,y))}","The set of clauses: {¬P(x,f(x)) ∨ Q(g(x)), ¬Q(f(x)) ∨ Q(g(x))}","None of the others is correct"],a:0,e:"∀x (∀y (¬P(x,y) ∧ ¬Q(y)) ∨ ∃z Q(z)) tras renombrar la x interior. Prenexa: ∀x∀y∃z, así que z/f(x,y). Distributiva: (¬P(x,y) ∨ Q(f(x,y))) ∧ (¬Q(y) ∨ Q(f(x,y)))."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 1",q:"We want to prove, using resolution, the soundness of { ∀x (A(x) ∨ B(x) → C(x)), ∃x A(x), ¬∃x B(x) } ⊨ ¬∀x ¬C(x). Indicate which set of formulas we would need to prove inconsistent.",o:["{¬A(x) ∨ C(x), ¬B(x) ∨ C(x), A(a), ¬B(x), C(b)}","None of the other answers is correct.","{¬A(x) ∨ C(x), ¬B(x) ∨ C(x), A(a), ¬B(x), ¬C(x)}","{A(x) ∨ ¬B(x) ∨ C(x), A(a), ¬B(x), ¬C(x)}"],a:2,ns:1,e:"A ∨ B → C ≡ (¬A ∨ C) ∧ (¬B ∨ C). ∃x A(x) da A(a). ¬∃x B(x) ≡ ∀x ¬B(x). La conclusión negada ¬¬∀x ¬C(x) ≡ ∀x ¬C(x) da ¬C(x)."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 2",q:"We want to prove, using resolution, the soundness of { ∀x (Q(x) ↔ R(x)), ∃x Q(x), ∀x (R(x) → ∃x P(x)) } ⊨ ∃x P(x). Indicate the set of formulas we would need to prove inconsistent.",o:["{¬Q(x) ∨ R(x), ¬R(x) ∨ Q(x), Q(a), ¬R(x) ∨ P(b), ¬P(x)}","{¬Q(x) ∨ R(x), ¬R(x) ∨ Q(x), Q(a), ¬R(x) ∨ P(b), P(c)}","None of the other answers is correct.","{¬Q(x) ∨ R(x), ¬R(x) ∨ Q(x), Q(a), ¬R(x) ∨ P(f(x)), P(b)}"],a:0,ns:1,e:"El ∃x P(x) interior no depende de la x exterior (es otra variable): puede salir delante y dar una constante, P(b). La conclusión negada da ¬P(x). b) y d) no niegan bien la conclusión. Con P(f(x)) también sería equisatisfacible, pero ninguna opción lo combina con ¬P(x)."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 1",m:1,q:"Let x, y, z be variables, a, b constants and f a function. Select the correct answers (there could be more than one):",o:["The most general unifier (m.g.u.) of the set {P(x,f(a)), P(f(z),b)} is {x/f(z), b/f(a)}","The set {P(x,f(x)), P(y,f(y)), P(f(a),f(a))} is not unifiable.","The most general unifier (m.g.u.) of the set {P(f(x),a,x), P(f(b),z,y)} is {x/b, z/a, y/x}","The most general unifier (m.g.u.) of the set {P(x,a), P(f(z),z)} is {x/f(z), z/a}"],a:[1],e:"a) f(a) y b chocan, y b/f(a) ni siquiera es una sustitución (b es constante). b) x = y = f(a) obliga a f(f(a)) = f(a): no unificable ✔. c) el mgu es {x/b, z/a, y/b}. d) falta componer: es {x/f(a), z/a}."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 1",q:"Let S = {¬q(a,Y) ∨ p(Y), p(a), t(X) ∨ ¬r(X) ∨ ¬s(f(X)), ¬p(Y) ∨ s(Y), ¬t(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X), t(X) ∨ ¬r(X) ∨ q(X,f(X))}. From S, is there a resolution derivation of □?",o:["Yes, and thus S is inconsistent.","No, and thus S is inconsistent.","Yes, and thus S is consistent.","No, and thus S is consistent."],a:0,ns:1,e:"p(a) da r(a). Con ¬t(a) y r(a), la última cláusula da q(a,f(a)); con la primera, p(f(a)), y después s(f(a)). La tercera cláusula con ¬t(a) y r(a) da ¬s(f(a)), y con s(f(a)) sale □."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 2",m:1,q:"Given the clauses C1: p(x,y) ∨ ¬q(x,x), C2: ¬p(f(a),a), C3: q(z,a) ∨ r(z), where x, y, z are variables, f a function, p, q, r predicates and a a constant, indicate the correct answers (there could be more than one):",o:["We cannot apply resolution on C1 and C3 since ¬q(x,x) and q(z,a) are not unifiable.","The resolvent of the clauses C1 and C2 would be ¬q(f(a),f(a))","The resolvent of the clauses C1 and C2 would be ¬q(x,x)","The resolvent of the clauses C1 and C3 would be p(a,y) ∨ r(a)"],a:[1,3],e:"q(x,x) y q(z,a) unifican con {x/a, z/a}, así que se puede resolver: p(a,y) ∨ r(a). C1 con C2: mgu {x/f(a), y/a}, que hay que aplicar al resto: ¬q(f(a),f(a))."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 3",m:1,q:"Consider the clauses C1: p(x,y) ∨ q(b,f(x)), C2: ¬p(a,a) ∨ ¬q(z,f(a)), C3: ¬p(f(t),b) ∨ ¬q(f(a),f(t)), where x, y, z, t are variables. Indicate the correct answers (there could be more than one):",o:["The clauses C1 and C3 only have two possible resolvents: q(b,f(x)) ∨ ¬q(f(a),f(t)) and p(x,y) ∨ ¬p(f(t),b)","The only possible resolvent for the clauses C1 and C3 would be: q(b,f(f(t))) ∨ ¬q(f(a),f(t))","The clauses C1 and C2 only have two possible resolvents: q(b,f(a)) ∨ ¬q(z,f(a)) and p(a,y) ∨ ¬p(a,a)","One of the possible resolvents of C1 and C2 is the empty clause"],a:[1,2],e:"C1-C3 sobre p: {x/f(t), y/b}, que da q(b,f(f(t))) ∨ ¬q(f(a),f(t)). Sobre q no: b y f(a) chocan. C1-C2 sobre p: {x/a, y/a}; sobre q: {z/b, x/a}. Nunca se eliminan dos pares a la vez, así que no sale □."},
{t:"q3",x:"Simulacro 3",q:"Given σ₁ = {x/g(z), y/z, z/f(y)} and σ₂ = {x/f(f(a)), y/f(a), t/z}, select one:",o:["σ₂σ₁ = {x/f(f(a)), y/f(a), t/f(y), z/f(f(a))}","σ₂σ₁ = {x/f(f(a)), y/f(a), t/f(y), x/g(z), y/z, z/f(y)}","σ₁σ₂ = {x/g(z), y/z, z/f(f(a)), t/z}","σ₁σ₂ = {x/g(z), y/z, z/f(y), t/z}"],a:2,ns:1,e:"σ₁σ₂: se aplica σ₂ a los términos de σ₁ (g(z) y z no cambian; f(y) pasa a f(f(a))) y se añade t/z, cuya variable no está en σ₁. σ₂σ₁ = {x/f(f(a)), y/f(a), t/f(y), z/f(y)}, así que a) falla en z."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"To prove { ∀X∀Y (p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y))), ∀X∀Y (q(X) ∨ r(X,Y)), ¬p(a) } ⊨ ∃X q(X) by resolution, the set of clauses is:",o:["{p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y)), q(X) ∨ r(X,Y), ¬p(a), ¬q(X)}","{p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y)), q(X) ∨ r(X,Y), ¬p(a), ¬q(a)}","{p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y)), q(X) ∨ r(X,Y), ¬p(a), q(b)}","{p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y)), q(X) ∧ r(X,Y), ¬p(a), ¬q(X)}"],a:0,e:"¬∃X q(X) ≡ ∀X ¬q(X): queda una variable, no una constante."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"In that refutation, resolving p(X) ∨ ¬r(X,f(Y)) with ¬p(a) gives:",o:["¬r(a,f(Y)), with mgu {X/a}","p(a) ∨ ¬r(a,f(Y))","¬r(X,f(Y)), with mgu { }","□"],a:0,e:"Paso 5 de la solución oficial."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 20/21",q:"Next, resolving ¬r(a,f(Y)) with q(X₂) ∨ r(X₂,Y₂) (variables renamed) gives:",o:["q(a), with mgu {X₂/a, Y₂/f(Y)}","q(X₂), with mgu { }","r(a,f(Y)) ∨ q(a)","Nothing: f(Y) and Y₂ do not unify"],a:0,e:"Y₂ es una variable y unifica con f(Y). Después q(a) con ¬q(X) da □ con {X/a}."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 19/20",q:"The clausal form of ∃x ¬(P(x) → ∃y R(y,x)) is:",o:["{P(a), ¬R(y,a)}","{P(a) ∧ ¬R(y,a)}","{¬P(x) ∨ R(f(x),x)}","{P(a), ¬R(b,a)}"],a:0,e:"∃x (P(x) ∧ ∀y ¬R(y,x)) → ∃x∀y → x/a. y es universal y queda como variable: d) es incorrecta."},
{t:"q3",x:"Examen 19/20",q:"The clausal form of the negated conclusion ¬∃x (P(x) ∧ ∀y ¬Q(y,x)) is:",o:["{¬P(x) ∨ Q(f(x),x)}","{¬P(x) ∨ Q(a,x)}","{¬P(a) ∨ Q(y,a)}","{P(x) ∧ ¬Q(f(x),x)}"],a:0,e:"∀x (¬P(x) ∨ ∃y Q(y,x)) → ∀x∃y → y/f(x)."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"A formula is in Skolem Normal Form (SNF) when (select all that apply):",o:["All the quantifiers are at the beginning","There are no existential quantifiers","The kernel is in conjunctive normal form","There are no function symbols"],a:[0,1,2],e:"La skolemización suele añadir símbolos de función, así que d) es falsa."},
{t:"q3",q:"Skolem's theorem states that every sentence F can be transformed into SKO(F) in SNF which is:",o:["Equisatisfiable with F, but not necessarily equivalent","Equivalent to F","Valid if and only if F is satisfiable","Always unsatisfiable"],a:0,e:"Todos los pasos conservan la equivalencia salvo eliminar los ∃, que solo conserva la satisfacibilidad. Basta para refutar: Φ ∪ {¬G} es inconsistente ⇔ SKO(Φ) ∪ SKO(¬G) es inconsistente."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Select the correct Skolemizations (there could be more than one):",o:["∀X∃Y p(X,Y) becomes ∀X p(X,f(X))","∃X∀Y p(X,Y) becomes ∀Y p(a,Y)","∀X∃Y p(X,Y) becomes ∀X p(X,a)","∃X∀Y p(X,Y) becomes ∀Y p(f(Y),Y)"],a:[0,1],e:"Y depende de X en a); en b) X no tiene ningún ∀ delante. c) y d) intercambian los casos."},
{t:"q3",q:"Order of the steps to obtain the clausal form of a predicate logic sentence:",o:["Eliminate ↔ and →, move ¬ inwards, rename variables, move quantifiers to the left, eliminate ∃ (Skolem), CNF, drop the ∀ and write the clauses","Eliminate ∃, eliminate →, move ¬ inwards, CNF, move quantifiers to the left","Move quantifiers to the left, eliminate →, eliminate ∃, move ¬ inwards, CNF","Eliminate →, CNF, eliminate ∃, move ¬ inwards"],a:0,ns:1,e:"Es la prueba constructiva del teorema de Skolem. Mover los cuantificadores antes de meter las negaciones cambiaría su tipo."},
{t:"q3",q:"Before moving the quantifiers of ∀X p(X) ∨ ∀X q(X) to the front we must:",o:["Rename one variable: ∀X p(X) ∨ ∀Y q(Y)","Merge them: ∀X (p(X) ∨ q(X))","Skolemize both","Nothing, it is already in prenex form"],a:0,e:"∀X (p(X) ∨ q(X)) no es equivalente. Con nombres distintos, la prenexa es ∀X∀Y (p(X) ∨ q(Y))."},
{t:"q3",q:"Following the procedure of the course, the clausal form of ∃X [p(X) → [∀Y (p(Y) → p(f(X,Y))) ∧ ¬∀Y (q(X,Y) → p(Y))]] is:",o:["{¬p(a) ∨ ¬p(Y) ∨ p(f(a,Y)), ¬p(a) ∨ q(a,g(Y)), ¬p(a) ∨ ¬p(g(Y))}","{¬p(a) ∨ ¬p(Y) ∨ p(f(a,Y)), ¬p(a) ∨ q(a,b), ¬p(a) ∨ ¬p(b)}","{¬p(X) ∨ ¬p(Y) ∨ p(f(X,Y)), q(X,Y), ¬p(Y)}","{¬p(a) ∨ ¬p(Y) ∨ p(f(a,Y)), ¬p(a) ∨ ¬q(a,g(Y)) ∨ p(g(Y))}"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo del tema: ¬∀Y (…) pasa a ∃Z (q(X,Z) ∧ ¬p(Z)) al renombrar; la prenexa es ∃X∀Y∃Z, así que X/a y Z/g(Y)."},
{t:"q3",q:"The clausal form of ∃X ∀Y ¬[¬p(X,Y) → ∀Z (q(Z) ∧ p(X,X))] is:",o:["{¬p(a,Y), ¬q(f(Y)) ∨ ¬p(a,a)}","{¬p(a,Y), ¬q(b) ∨ ¬p(a,a)}","{¬p(X,Y), ¬q(Z) ∨ ¬p(X,X)}","{p(a,Y) ∨ q(f(Y)), p(a,Y) ∨ p(a,a)}"],a:0,e:"¬[p(X,Y) ∨ ∀Z (…)] = ¬p(X,Y) ∧ ∃Z (¬q(Z) ∨ ¬p(X,X)). Prenexa ∃X∀Y∃Z: X/a y Z/f(Y)."},
{t:"q3",q:"The clausal form of ∀X [∃Y (p(X,Y) → r(X,Y)) → ∃Y (q(Y) → s(Y))] is:",o:["{p(X,Y) ∨ ¬q(f(X,Y)) ∨ s(f(X,Y)), ¬r(X,Y) ∨ ¬q(f(X,Y)) ∨ s(f(X,Y))}","{p(X,Y) ∨ ¬q(f(X)) ∨ s(f(X)), ¬r(X,Y) ∨ ¬q(f(X)) ∨ s(f(X))}","{¬p(X,Y) ∨ r(X,Y) ∨ ¬q(a) ∨ s(a)}","{p(X,f(X)) ∨ ¬q(Y) ∨ s(Y), ¬r(X,f(X)) ∨ ¬q(Y) ∨ s(Y)}"],a:0,e:"¬∃Y (…) pasa a ∀Y (p(X,Y) ∧ ¬r(X,Y)); tras renombrar, la prenexa es ∀X∀Y∃Z y Z/f(X,Y)."},
{t:"q3",q:"Transforming the premise ∃X (p(X) ∨ t(X)) into clausal form, when the constant a already appears in other clauses, we get:",o:["p(b) ∨ t(b), with a new constant","p(a) ∨ t(a)","p(X) ∨ t(X)","p(f(X)) ∨ t(f(X))"],a:0,e:"La constante de Skolem tiene que ser nueva. Es el ejemplo del algoritmo de resolución del tema."},
{t:"q3",q:"Which of the following is NOT a valid substitution?",o:["{X/f(X)}","{X/f(Y), Y/a}","{X/b, Y/a, Z/f(U)}","{X/Y}"],a:0,e:"Ninguna variable puede sustituirse por un término que la contenga."},
{t:"q3",q:"Applying θ = {X/g(Y)} to p(X,W,f(X)) gives:",o:["p(g(Y),W,f(g(Y)))","p(g(Y),W,f(X))","p(X,W,f(g(Y)))","p(g(Y),g(Y),f(g(Y)))"],a:0,e:"Todas las apariciones de X se sustituyen por el mismo término."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Let σ₁ = {Z/g(X,Y)} and σ₂ = {X/a, Y/b, W/c, Z/d}. Select the correct statements (there could be more than one):",o:["σ₁σ₂ = {Z/g(a,b), X/a, Y/b, W/c}","σ₂σ₁ = σ₂","σ₁σ₂ = {Z/g(a,b), X/a, Y/b, W/c, Z/d}","σ₁σ₂ = σ₂σ₁"],a:[0,1],e:"Ejemplo del tema. En σ₁σ₂ no se añade Z/d porque Z ya está en σ₁. En σ₂σ₁, σ₁ no cambia ningún término de σ₂ y su único par (Z) ya está."},
{t:"q3",q:"The composition σ₁σ₂ is computed by:",o:["Applying σ₂ to the terms of σ₁ and adding the pairs of σ₂ whose variable does not occur in σ₁","Applying σ₁ to the terms of σ₂ and adding every pair of σ₁","The union of both sets of pairs","Applying σ₂ to the variables of σ₁"],a:0,e:"Cumple Eσ₁σ₂ = (Eσ₁)σ₂. No es conmutativa."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Select the unifiable sets (there could be more than one):",o:["{p(f(X),Z), p(Y,a)}","{p(f(X),a), p(Y,f(U))}","{p(f(X),g(U,Z)), p(Y,g(V,a))}","{p(f(a),g(X)), p(Y,Y)}"],a:[0,2],e:"a) {Y/f(X), Z/a}. c) {Y/f(X), U/V, Z/a}. b) a y f(U) chocan. d) Y tendría que ser f(a) y g(X) a la vez."},
{t:"q3",q:"The mgu of {p(f(Z),g(U,Z)), p(Y,g(V,a))} is:",o:["{Y/f(a), U/V, Z/a}","{Y/f(Z), U/V, Z/a}","{Y/f(a), V/U}","The set is not unifiable"],a:0,e:"Y/f(Z), U/V y Z/a; al componer, Y/f(Z) pasa a Y/f(a). b) es el error de no componer: no unifica."},
{t:"q3",q:"The mgu of {p(a,X,h(g(Z))), p(Z,h(Y),h(Y))} is:",o:["{Z/a, X/h(g(a)), Y/g(a)}","{Z/a, X/h(Y), Y/g(Z)}","{Z/a, X/h(g(Z)), Y/g(a)}","The set is not unifiable"],a:0,e:"D = {a, Z} → Z/a; D = {X, h(Y)} → X/h(Y); D = {g(a), Y} → Y/g(a), y al componer X/h(Y) pasa a X/h(g(a))."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Which sets are NOT unifiable? (there could be more than one)",o:["{p(X,f(a),g(g(Y))), p(Z,f(Z),g(Y))}","{p(f(a),g(X)), p(Y,Y)}","{p(a,X,g(g(Z))), p(Z,h(Y),g(Y))}","{p(X,f(X),f(a)), p(g(Y),Z,Z)}"],a:[0,1,3],e:"a) acaba pidiendo Y = g(Y) (occurs check). b) Y = f(a) y Y = g(X). d) Z = f(g(Y)) y Z = f(a): g(Y) choca con a. c) tiene mgu {Z/a, X/h(g(a)), Y/g(a)}."},
{t:"q3",q:"Is {p(f(X),h(Y),a), p(f(X),Z,a), p(f(X),h(Y),b)} unifiable?",o:["No: the third arguments a and b are different constants","Yes, with {Z/h(Y)}","Yes, with {Z/h(Y), a/b}","Yes, with { }"],a:0,e:"Dos constantes distintas nunca unifican, y a/b no es una sustitución."},
{t:"q3",q:"mgu{p(X,Y), p(Y,f(X))} fails. If the two atoms come from different clauses, what should we do?",o:["Rename the variables of one clause, e.g. p(Y₁,f(X₁)), whose mgu with p(X,Y) is {X/Y₁, Y/f(X₁)}","Nothing: they will never unify","Use {X/Y, Y/f(X)}","Replace X by a constant"],a:0,e:"Las variables de cláusulas distintas son independientes: antes de resolver se renombran."},
{t:"q3",q:"Why is {p(X,X), p(Y,f(Y))} not unifiable?",o:["After {X/Y} we must unify Y with f(Y), and Y occurs in f(Y)","Because p has two arguments","Because X and Y are different variables","It is unifiable with {X/f(Y), Y/f(Y)}"],a:0,e:"Comprobación de ocurrencia (occurs check)."},
{t:"q3",q:"In the unification algorithm, μᵢ₊₁ is obtained as:",o:["μᵢδ, the composition of μᵢ with the new binding δ","μᵢ ∪ δ, without modifying μᵢ","δμᵢ","δ alone"],a:0,e:"«Remember: it's a composition». Por eso, en el ejemplo, X/f(Z) pasa a X/f(a)."},
{t:"q3",q:"The disagreement set of {p(X,a,f(g(Y))), p(f(Z),Z,f(U))} is:",o:["{X, f(Z)}","{a, Z}","{g(Y), U}","{X, Z, U}"],a:0,e:"Primera posición, de izquierda a derecha, en la que las expresiones difieren."},
{t:"q3",q:"In general resolution, C₁ = G ∨ ¬E₁ ∨ ¬E₃ and C₂ = H ∨ E₂ (E₁, E₂, E₃ atoms of the same predicate) can be resolved obtaining:",o:["Gσ ∨ Hσ, with σ = mgu(E₁ ∪ E₂ ∪ E₃)","G ∨ H, without any substitution","Gσ ∨ ¬E₃σ ∨ Hσ, with σ = mgu(E₁ ∪ E₂ ∪ E₃)","Nothing: only one literal can be removed"],a:0,e:"Si varios literales de una cláusula unifican con el complementario, se eliminan todos a la vez."},
{t:"q3",q:"From ¬dog(X) ∨ animal(X), dog(bobby), ¬animal(Y) ∨ die(Y) and ¬die(bobby), which resolvent comes from the first and the third clause?",o:["¬dog(Y) ∨ die(Y)","¬dog(X) ∨ ¬die(X)","animal(Y) ∨ die(Y)","□"],a:0,e:"mgu{animal(X), animal(Y)} = {X/Y}. Después dog(bobby) da die(bobby) y ¬die(bobby) da □."},
{t:"q3",q:"To prove {∀X (q(X) ∨ ¬p(X)), ∀X (r(X) ∨ ¬q(X)), p(f(a))} ⊨ ∃X r(f(X)) by resolution, the set of clauses to refute is:",o:["{q(X) ∨ ¬p(X), r(X) ∨ ¬q(X), p(f(a)), ¬r(f(X))}","{q(X) ∨ ¬p(X), r(X) ∨ ¬q(X), p(f(a)), ¬r(f(b))}","{q(X) ∨ ¬p(X), r(X) ∨ ¬q(X), p(f(a)), r(f(X))}","{q(X) ∨ ¬p(X), r(X) ∨ ¬q(X), ¬p(f(a)), ¬r(f(X))}"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo del tema: la conclusión negada ∀X ¬r(f(X)) da ¬r(f(X))."},
{t:"q3",q:"Before resolving r(X) ∨ ¬q(X) with ¬r(f(X)) we should:",o:["Rename the variables of one clause, e.g. ¬r(f(X₁)), because both contain variables","Replace X by a constant","Nothing: X is the same variable in both clauses","Factor both clauses"],a:0,e:"Paso del algoritmo de resolución: renombrar si las dos cláusulas tienen variables."},
{t:"q3",q:"In {s(X) ∨ ¬q(Y) ∨ ¬r(X,Y), ¬p(X) ∨ q(X), p(b), r(a,b), ¬s(a)}, resolving ¬s(a) with the first clause gives:",o:["¬q(Y) ∨ ¬r(a,Y), with {X/a}","s(a) ∨ ¬q(Y)","¬q(a) ∨ ¬r(a,a)","□"],a:0,e:"Ejercicio de resolución del tema."},
{t:"q3",q:"Which sequence refutes {s(X) ∨ ¬q(Y) ∨ ¬r(X,Y), ¬p(X) ∨ q(X), p(b), r(a,b), ¬s(a)}?",o:["¬q(Y) ∨ ¬r(a,Y), then ¬q(b) (with r(a,b)), then ¬p(b) (with ¬p(X) ∨ q(X)), then □ (with p(b))","None: the set is consistent","¬q(a), then ¬p(a), then □","s(a), then □"],a:0,e:"Cada paso elimina un par de literales complementarios tras unificar."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Select the true statements about resolution strategies (there could be more than one):",o:["The support set contains the clauses from the negated conclusion and resolvents with at least one parent in the support set.","SLD resolution, used by Prolog, is a particularization of the support set strategy.","The breadth-first strategy computes all resolvents of each level.","A complete strategy may fail to find a contradiction that exists."],a:[0,1,2],e:"Una estrategia es completa si encuentra la contradicción siempre que exista."},
{t:"q3",q:"For {∃X∀Y p(X,Y)} ⊨ ∀Y∃X p(X,Y), the clauses to refute are:",o:["{p(a,Y), ¬p(X,b)}","{p(X,Y), ¬p(X,Y)}","{p(a,Y), ¬p(X,f(X))}","{p(a,b), ¬p(a,b)}"],a:0,e:"Conclusión negada: ∃Y∀X ¬p(X,Y) → Y/b, una constante nueva. mgu {X/a, Y/b} → □."},
{t:"q3",q:"For { ∃X (p(X) ∨ q(X)), ∀X (p(X) → r(X,X)), ¬∃X q(X) } ⊨ ∃X r(X,X), the clauses to refute are:",o:["{p(a) ∨ q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X,X), ¬q(X), ¬r(X,X)}","{p(X) ∨ q(X), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X,X), ¬q(a), ¬r(a,a)}","{p(a) ∨ q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X,X), q(X), r(X,X)}","{p(a), q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X,X), ¬q(X), ¬r(X,X)}"],a:0,e:"Después: p(a) ∨ q(a) con ¬q(X) da p(a); con ¬p(X) ∨ r(X,X), r(a,a); con ¬r(X,X), □."},
{t:"q3",q:"For {∀X (r(X) → q(X)), ∃X (p(X) ∧ ¬q(X))} ⊨ ∃X (p(X) ∧ ¬r(X)), the clauses to refute are:",o:["{¬r(X) ∨ q(X), p(a), ¬q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X)}","{¬r(X) ∨ q(X), p(a) ∧ ¬q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X)}","{r(X) ∨ ¬q(X), p(a), ¬q(a), ¬p(X) ∨ r(X)}","{¬r(X) ∨ q(X), p(a), ¬q(b), p(X) ∧ ¬r(X)}"],a:0,e:"La conjunción da dos cláusulas: p(a) y ¬q(a). La conclusión negada ∀X (¬p(X) ∨ r(X)) da una."},
{t:"q3",q:"The clausal form of ¬∀X ¬p(X) is:",o:["{p(a)}","{p(X)}","{¬p(X)}","{¬p(a)}"],a:0,e:"¬∀X ¬p(X) ≡ ∃X p(X) ≡sat p(a)."},
{t:"q3",m:1,q:"Which are resolvents of C₁ = p(X) ∨ q(X) and C₂ = ¬p(a) ∨ ¬q(b)? (there could be more than one)",o:["q(a) ∨ ¬q(b)","p(b) ∨ ¬p(a)","□","q(X) ∨ ¬q(b)"],a:[0,1],e:"Sobre p: {X/a}. Sobre q: {X/b}. Hay que aplicar el mgu a todo el resolvente."},
{t:"q3",q:"The set {p(X) ∨ q(X), ¬p(a), ¬q(a)} is:",o:["Inconsistent: p(X) ∨ q(X) with ¬p(a) gives q(a), and q(a) with ¬q(a) gives □","Consistent: X can take a value different from a","Inconsistent only if a is the only constant","Not in clausal form"],a:0,e:"Las variables de las cláusulas están cuantificadas universalmente: valen también para a."},
{t:"q3",q:"In the conversion to clausal form, writing ≡sat after eliminating existential quantifiers means:",o:["The new formula is equisatisfiable with the previous one, not equivalent","The formulas are equivalent","The formula is satisfiable","The formula is valid"],a:0,e:"Lo verás en las soluciones oficiales (≡SAT)."},
{t:"q3",q:"General resolution needs unification because:",o:["{∀X p(X), ¬p(a)} is inconsistent, but p(X) and ¬p(a) are not complementary until X is particularized to a","Clauses cannot contain variables","Propositional resolution does not use clausal form","Unification removes the existential quantifiers"],a:0,e:"Unificar es encontrar la particularización mínima que hace complementarios dos literales."},

/* ===================== q4 · Deducción natural (L1) y propiedades ===================== */
{t:"q4",x:"Examen 19/20",m:1,q:"Look at the proof of {∃X p(X), ∀X (q(X) → ¬p(X))} ⊢ ∃X ¬q(X) below. Select the correct statements about the missing parts (there could be more than one):",c:"1.  ∃X p(X)                  Premise\n2.  ∀X (q(X) → ¬p(X))        Premise\n┌ 3.  p(a), a free           Assumption\n│ 4.  q(a) → ¬p(a)           ??\n│ ┌ 5.  q(a)                 Assumption\n│ │ 6.  ¬p(a)                →E 4,5\n│ └ 7.  ??                   ∧I 3,6\n│ 8.  ¬q(a)                  ??\n└ 9.  ∃X ¬q(X)               ∃I 8\n10. ∃X ¬q(X)                 ??",o:["Line 4 is justified by ∀E 2","Line 7 is p(a) ∧ ¬p(a)","Line 8 is justified by ¬E 5-7","Line 10 is justified by ∃E 1,3-9"],a:[0,1,3],e:"Solución oficial. La línea 8 es ¬I 5-7: se supuso q(a) y se concluye su negación. ¬E sería suponer ¬q(a) para concluir q(a)."},
{t:"q4",x:"Simulacro 1",m:1,q:"Given the following incomplete natural deduction proof, select the correct answers (there could be more than one).",c:"1.  ¬∀x (¬p(x))      Premise\n┌ 2.  ??             Assumption\n│ ┌ 3.  ??           Assumption\n│ │ ┌ 4.  ??         Assumption\n│ │ │ 5.  ??         ??\n│ │ └ 6.  ??         ??\n│ └ 7.  ??           ??\n│ 8.  ??             ??\n└ 9.  ??             ??\n10. ∃x (p(x))        ??",o:["The justification for step 10 is ¬E 2-9","The content of step 8 is ∀x (¬p(x))","The content of step 9 is ∃x (p(x))","The justification for step 10 is ∃E 2-9"],a:[0,1],e:"2 ¬∃x p(x) (sup.), 3 (t) free, 4 p(t) (sup.), 5 ∃x p(x) (∃I 4), 6 ∃x p(x) ∧ ¬∃x p(x) (∧I 2,5), 7 ¬p(t) (¬I 4-6), 8 ∀x ¬p(x) (∀I 3-7), 9 ∀x ¬p(x) ∧ ¬∀x ¬p(x) (∧I 1,8), 10 ∃x p(x) (¬E 2-9)."},
{t:"q4",x:"Simulacro 2",m:1,q:"Given the following incomplete natural deduction proof, select the correct answers (there could be more than one).",c:"1.  ∃x p(x)                 Premise\n2.  ∀x∃y (p(x) → r(x,y))   Premise\n┌ 3.  ??                    Assumption\n│ 4.  ??                    ??\n│ ┌ 5.  ??                  Assumption\n│ │ 6.  ??                  ??\n│ └ 7.  ??                  ??\n│ 8.  ??                    ??\n└ 9.  ??                    ??\n10. ∃x∃y r(x,y)             ??",o:["The justification for step 7 is →E 4,6","The content of step 4 is p(a) → r(a,b)","The justification for step 10 is ∃E 1,3-9","The content of step 6 is r(a,b)"],a:[2,3],e:"3 p(a), a free; 4 ∃y (p(a) → r(a,y)) (∀E 2); 5 p(a) → r(a,b), b free; 6 r(a,b) (→E 3,5); 7 ∃y r(a,y) (∃I 6); 8 ∃y r(a,y) (∃E 4,5-7); 9 ∃x∃y r(x,y) (∃I 8); 10 ∃E 1,3-9."},
{t:"q4",x:"Simulacro 3",m:1,q:"Given the following incomplete natural deduction proof, select the correct answers (there could be more than one).",c:"1.  ∃x (p(x) ∨ q(x))        Premise\n2.  ∀x (p(x) → r(x,x))      Premise\n3.  ∀x (q(x) → s(x))        Premise\n┌ 4.  ??                    Assumption\n│ ┌ 5.  ??                  Assumption\n│ │ 6.  ??                  ??\n│ │ 7.  ??                  ??\n│ └ 8.  ??                  ??\n│ 9.  ??                    ??\n│ ┌ 10. ??                  Assumption\n│ │ 11. ??                  ??\n│ │ 12. ??                  ??\n│ └ 13. ??                  ??\n│ 14. ??                    ??\n│ 15. ??                    ??\n└ 16. ??                    ??\n17. ∃x (r(x,x) ∨ s(x))      ??",o:["The content of step 13 is r(a,a) ∨ s(a)","The justification for step 15 is ∨E 4, 9, 14","The justification for step 8 is ∨I 7","The justification for step 17 is ¬E 4-16"],a:[0,1,2],e:"4 p(a) ∨ q(a), a free; 5 p(a); 6 p(a) → r(a,a) (∀E 2); 7 r(a,a) (→E 5,6); 8 r(a,a) ∨ s(a) (∨I 7); 9 →I 5-8; 10 q(a); 11 ∀E 3; 12 s(a); 13 r(a,a) ∨ s(a) (∨I 12); 14 →I 10-13; 15 ∨E 4,9,14; 16 ∃I 15; 17 ∃E 1,4-16."},
{t:"q4",q:"The rule ∀E allows us to derive from ∀X A(X):",o:["A(a) for any term a","A(t) only if t is free","∃X A(X) directly, without intermediate steps","A(X) with X free in a new box"],a:0,e:"Particularizar un universal: se puede usar tantas veces como haga falta."},
{t:"q4",q:"To derive ∀X A(X) with ∀I we must:",o:["Open a box with a term t free (not appearing in any previous open box), derive A(t) and close the box","Derive A(a) for some constant a of the premises","Derive A(t) for some t that appears in the premises","Assume ∀X A(X) and reach a contradiction"],a:0,e:"La caja empieza con «(t) free» y se justifica como ∀I con su rango: ∀I 4-7."},
{t:"q4",q:"The rule ∃I allows us to:",o:["Derive ∃X A(X) from A(a)","Derive A(a) from ∃X A(X)","Derive ∀X A(X) from A(t) with t free","Derive ∃X A(X) from ¬A(a)"],a:0,e:"Si un elemento concreto cumple A, existe alguno que lo cumple."},
{t:"q4",m:1,q:"In the rule ∃E (from ∃X A(X) and a box that assumes A(t), t free, and derives B, conclude B), which conditions must hold? (there could be more than one)",o:["t must be free: it cannot appear in any previous open box","t must not appear in B","B must be ∃X A(X)","t must be a constant already used in the premises"],a:[0,1],e:"La condición t ∉ B del cuadro de reglas: lo que se saca de la caja no puede depender del testigo elegido."},
{t:"q4",q:"In natural deduction, “t free” means:",o:["The term t cannot appear in any previous open box","t is a variable","t does not appear in the conclusion of the proof","t is not a function symbol"],a:0,e:"Definición del cuadro de reglas."},
{t:"q4",q:"Why is the following proof of {∃X P(X), ∃X Q(X)} ⊢ ∃X (P(X) ∧ Q(X)) incorrect?",c:"1.  ∃X P(X)                Premise\n2.  ∃X Q(X)                Premise\n┌ 3.  P(a), a free         Assumption\n│ ┌ 4.  Q(a), a free       Assumption\n│ │ 5.  P(a) ∧ Q(a)        ∧I 3,4\n│ └ 6.  ∃X (P(X) ∧ Q(X))   ∃I 5\n│ 7.  ∃X (P(X) ∧ Q(X))     ∃E 2,4-6\n└\n8.  ∃X (P(X) ∧ Q(X))       ∃E 1,3-7",o:["In line 4, Q(a) is assumed with a free, but a already appears in the open box of line 3","Line 5 should be justified by ∧E","∃I cannot be applied to P(a) ∧ Q(a)","There is nothing wrong: the reasoning is sound"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo de mal uso del tema. El testigo de ∃X Q(X) tiene que ser nuevo; y de hecho el razonamiento no es correcto (hay estudiantes y hay trabajadores, pero quizá ningún estudiante trabajador)."},
{t:"q4",q:"In the proof of {∀X∀Y (P(X) → Q(Y)), ∃X P(X)} ⊢ ∀Y Q(Y), the box 3-8 assumes P(t₁), t₁ free, and the box 5-7 introduces t₂ free. How is the last line ∀Y Q(Y) justified?",o:["∃E 2,3-8","∀I 5-7","∀E 1","∃I 8"],a:0,e:"Dentro de la caja de ∃E se obtiene ∀Y Q(Y) por ∀I 5-7 (línea 8). Como no contiene t₁, se puede sacar con ∃E."},
{t:"q4",q:"Which of the following can be proved by natural deduction?",o:["{∃X∀Y P(X,Y)} ⊢ ∀Y∃X P(X,Y)","{∀Y∃X P(X,Y)} ⊢ ∃X∀Y P(X,Y)","{∃X P(X), ∃X Q(X)} ⊢ ∃X (P(X) ∧ Q(X))","{∀X (P(X) ∨ Q(X))} ⊢ ∀X P(X) ∨ ∀X Q(X)"],a:0,e:"La deducción natural es correcta: solo demuestra consecuencias lógicas, y b), c) y d) no lo son."},
{t:"q4",q:"In the proof of {∀X (R(X) → Q(X)), ∃X (P(X) ∧ ¬Q(X))} ⊢ ∃X (P(X) ∧ ¬R(X)), after assuming P(t) ∧ ¬Q(t) with t free, how is ¬R(t) obtained?",o:["Assuming R(t), deriving Q(t) with →E and Q(t) ∧ ¬Q(t), then ¬I","With ∀E directly from the first premise","With ∧E from P(t) ∧ ¬Q(t)","Assuming ¬R(t) and applying ¬E"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo 13 del tema. Después ∧I da P(t) ∧ ¬R(t), ∃I y ∃E 2,3-12."},
{t:"q4",q:"To prove {∃X (P(X) ∨ Q(X))} ⊢ ∃X P(X) ∨ ∃X Q(X), inside the box that assumes P(t) ∨ Q(t) (t free) we use:",o:["∨E with P(t) → (∃X P(X) ∨ ∃X Q(X)) and Q(t) → (∃X P(X) ∨ ∃X Q(X))","∀I","¬E","∃E directly on P(t) ∨ Q(t)"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo 9: dos cajas (P(t) y Q(t)) con ∃I y ∨I, →I para cerrarlas y ∨E; al final ∃E 1,2-11."},
{t:"q4",q:"In {∀X (P(X) ∨ Q(X)), ∀X (P(X) → R(X)), ∀X (Q(X) → R(X))} ⊢ ∀X R(X), inside the box with t free, R(t) is obtained by:",o:["∨E from P(t) ∨ Q(t), P(t) → R(t) and Q(t) → R(t)","→E from P(t) → R(t) alone","∀E 2","∃E 1"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo 12: tres ∀E, ∨E 5,6,7 y ∀I 4-8."},
{t:"q4",q:"In the proof of {¬∃X P(X)} ⊢ ∀X ¬P(X), which contradiction is reached after assuming P(t)?",o:["∃X P(X) ∧ ¬∃X P(X)","P(t) ∧ ¬P(t)","∀X P(X) ∧ ¬∀X P(X)","None: ∀I is applied directly"],a:0,e:"P(t) da ∃X P(X) por ∃I, que choca con la premisa. ¬I da ¬P(t) y ∀I cierra la caja de t."},
{t:"q4",q:"In the proof of {∀X P(X) ∧ ∀X Q(X)} ⊢ ∀X (P(X) ∧ Q(X)), the line P(t) ∧ Q(t) inside the box with t free is justified by:",o:["∧I","∀E","∀I","∧E"],a:0,e:"P(t) y Q(t) salen por ∀E; se juntan con ∧I y la caja se cierra con ∀I."},
{t:"q4",q:"From the premise P(a), can we conclude ∀X P(X) with ∀I?",o:["No: ∀I needs A(t) for an arbitrary t introduced in a box, not for a particular constant","Yes, directly","Yes, using ∃I first","Only if a is the only element of the domain"],a:0,e:"Que a cumpla P no dice nada del resto de elementos."},
{t:"q4",q:"Predicate logic is:",o:["Semidecidable: if Γ ⊨ Q a proof can be found in finite time, but if not, no algorithm is guaranteed to terminate","Decidable, like propositional logic","Undecidable in both directions","Decidable using truth tables"],a:0,e:"Propiedades de L1 del tema."},
{t:"q4",m:1,q:"Select the true statements (there could be more than one):",o:["Propositional logic is a logic of order 0.","Predicate logic is a logic of order 1.","Temporal logic and fuzzy logic are extensions of classical logic.","Predicate logic is less expressive than propositional logic."],a:[0,1,2],e:"Diapositiva «Other logics?». L1 es más expresiva que L0."},
{t:"q4",q:"General resolution and natural deduction in predicate logic are:",o:["Sound and complete","Sound but not complete","Complete but not sound","Neither sound nor complete"],a:0,e:"Φ ⊨ G si y solo si Φ ∪ {¬G} ⊢ □, y lo mismo con deducción natural."},
{t:"q4",q:"In {∀X (P(X) → Q(X)), P(a)} ⊢ ∃X Q(X): 3. P(a) → Q(a) by ∀E 1; 4. Q(a) by →E 2,3; 5. ∃X Q(X) by…",o:["∃I 4","∃E 4","∀I 4","→I 3-4"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo 5 del tema."},
{t:"q4",q:"In {∀X (P(X) → Q(X)), ∃X P(X)} ⊢ ∃X Q(X), why do we need ∃E instead of using P(a) directly?",o:["Because the premise only says that some element verifies P: we assume P(t) with t free and close the box with ∃E","Because ∃X P(X) is false","Because ∀E cannot be applied to P(t)","We don't: P(a) follows from ∃X P(X) by ∃I"],a:0,e:"Ejemplo 6: no sabemos qué elemento es, así que razonamos con uno arbitrario."},
{t:"q4",m:1,q:"Look at the proof of {∀X∀Y (P(X) → Q(Y)), ∃X P(X)} ⊢ ∀Y Q(Y). Select the correct statements (there could be more than one):",c:"1.  ∀X∀Y (P(X) → Q(Y))      Premise\n2.  ∃X P(X)                 Premise\n┌ 3.  P(t₁), t₁ free        Assumption\n│ 4.  ∀Y (P(t₁) → Q(Y))     ∀E 1\n│ ┌ 5.  (t₂) free\n│ │ 6.  ??                  ??\n│ └ 7.  Q(t₂)               →E 3,6\n└ 8.  ∀Y Q(Y)               ??\n9.  ∀Y Q(Y)                 ∃E 2,3-8",o:["Line 6 is P(t₁) → Q(t₂), justified by ∀E 4","Line 8 is justified by ∀I 5-7","Line 4 should be justified by ∃E 2","Line 7 could be obtained by ∀E 1 directly"],a:[0,1],e:"Ejemplo 10 del tema. Q(t₂) necesita →E con P(t₁), que está en la línea 3."},
{t:"q4",m:1,q:"Look at the proof of {∃X∀Y P(X,Y)} ⊢ ∀Y∃X P(X,Y). Select the correct statements (there could be more than one):",c:"1.  ∃X∀Y P(X,Y)          Premise\n┌ 2.  ∀Y P(a,Y), a free  Assumption\n│ ┌ 3.  (b) free\n│ │ 4.  P(a,b)           ??\n│ └ 5.  ∃X P(X,b)        ??\n└ 6.  ∀Y∃X P(X,Y)        ∀I 3-5\n7.  ∀Y∃X P(X,Y)          ??",o:["Line 4 is justified by ∀E 2","Line 5 is justified by ∃I 4","Line 7 is justified by ∀I 1,2-6","Line 6 should be justified by ∃E 3-5"],a:[0,1],e:"Ejemplo 11 del tema: la línea 7 es ∃E 1,2-6."},
{t:"q4",q:"Which rule do you usually apply to a premise ∀X A(X), as many times as needed and with different terms?",o:["∀E","∀I","∃E","∃I"],a:0,e:"En los ejemplos aparece justo después de abrir una caja con un término libre."},
{t:"q4",q:"In an ∃E box, what may be assumed in its first line?",o:["A(t) with t free, where ∃X A(X) is the formula being eliminated","Any formula with free variables","The negation of the conclusion","∀X A(X)"],a:0,e:"Y la caja se cierra copiando una fórmula B que no contenga t: ∃E línea_del_∃, rango."}
];
